1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,640
Welcome to PackBridge.

2
00:00:01,640 --> 00:00:06,720
This walkthrough shows a new Shopify B2B merchant how to go from install to the first normalized

3
00:00:06,720 --> 00:00:08,800
order in about 5 minutes.

4
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:12,400
Start in the Shopify App Store and install PackBridge into the store.

5
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:16,640
Shopify sends you through OAuth so you can approve the read-only permissions PackBridge

6
00:00:16,640 --> 00:00:22,800
needs, orders, products, companies, and customers for B2B purchasing context.

7
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:28,040
PackBridge does not request write scopes, and it does not change orders, products, or

8
00:00:28,040 --> 00:00:30,080
customers in Shopify.

9
00:00:30,080 --> 00:00:33,040
After OAuth, you land on the PackBridge dashboard.

10
00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:35,280
The first job is the initial sync.

11
00:00:35,280 --> 00:00:41,400
PackBridge mirrors B2B companies, company locations, products, and variants into its own database

12
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:44,200
so the admin can resolve pack rules quickly.

13
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:49,800
The dashboard confirms the latest sync time, active rule count, processed orders, and recent

14
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:51,640
normalization jobs.

15
00:00:51,640 --> 00:00:53,920
Next, create your first pack rule.

16
00:00:53,920 --> 00:00:56,300
A rule can apply to all companies.

17
00:00:56,300 --> 00:01:01,360
One company, one company location, a product, or a specific variant.

18
00:01:01,360 --> 00:01:03,640
Choose the most specific scope you need.

19
00:01:03,640 --> 00:01:04,920
Set the pack size.

20
00:01:04,920 --> 00:01:11,360
Then choose the downstream unit code your ERP expects, such as case, inner, or pallet.

21
00:01:11,360 --> 00:01:15,160
Enforcement mode controls what happens when the ordered quantity is not divisible by the

22
00:01:15,160 --> 00:01:16,480
pack size.

23
00:01:16,480 --> 00:01:21,660
Warn flags the order, hold marks the job for review, normalize only emits the translation

24
00:01:21,660 --> 00:01:23,140
and records the warning.

25
00:01:23,140 --> 00:01:29,660
For larger catalogs, use the CSV import flow, download the template, fill in company name,

26
00:01:29,660 --> 00:01:35,980
company location name, SKU, pack size, downstream unit code, and enforcement mode, then upload

27
00:01:35,980 --> 00:01:36,980
the file.

28
00:01:36,980 --> 00:01:40,060
PackBridge previews every row before writing rules.

29
00:01:40,060 --> 00:01:45,260
Valid rows are ready to import, and invalid rows explain exactly what needs to be fixed,

30
00:01:45,260 --> 00:01:49,780
such as an unknown SKU or a location that does not belong to the selected company.

31
00:01:49,780 --> 00:01:51,500
Now configure delivery.

32
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:58,380
On settings, paste the HTTPS endpoint for your ERP, EDI, middleware, or warehouse system.

33
00:01:58,380 --> 00:02:03,100
PackBridge signs every outbound request with the signing secret shown on this page.

34
00:02:03,100 --> 00:02:08,100
Your server verifies the X-PackBridge-Signature header by computing an HMAC over the raw

35
00:02:08,100 --> 00:02:11,380
request body. With rules and settings in place.

36
00:02:11,380 --> 00:02:13,900
Place a B2B test order in Shopify.

37
00:02:13,900 --> 00:02:16,060
When the orders create webhook arrives.

38
00:02:16,060 --> 00:02:19,300
PackBridge resolves the purchasing company and location.

39
00:02:19,300 --> 00:02:24,940
Chooses the most specific matching rule, validates divisibility, and writes a normalization event

40
00:02:24,940 --> 00:02:26,580
for each line item.

41
00:02:26,580 --> 00:02:28,780
Open the jobs page to audit the result.

42
00:02:28,780 --> 00:02:33,060
The list shows completed, held, mixed, and failed jobs.

43
00:02:33,060 --> 00:02:39,580
Open a job detail page to see the order summary, line item inputs, resolved output quantities,

44
00:02:39,580 --> 00:02:43,380
downstream units, validation warnings, and delivery status.

45
00:02:43,380 --> 00:02:48,500
If the endpoint returns a temporary 500, PackBridge retries and records the successful

46
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:49,500
recovery.

47
00:02:49,500 --> 00:02:52,380
Finally, verify the payload at your endpoint.

48
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:57,780
A normalized line contains the original input quantity, the resolved pack size, the output

49
00:02:57,780 --> 00:03:03,020
quantity, the downstream unit, and the order context your downstream system needs.

50
00:03:03,020 --> 00:03:08,140
The delivery ID and HMAC signature make the payload traceable and verifiable.

51
00:03:08,140 --> 00:03:13,900
That is the core PackBridge setup: install, sync, create or import rules, configure a signed

52
00:03:13,900 --> 00:03:19,700
webhook, place a B2B order, and confirm the ERP receives clean pack-unit JSON.

53
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:25,300
For help, contact support at support at packbridge.app, or use the documentation link from the

54
00:03:25,300 --> 00:03:25,800
listing.
